          "verdict": "malicious",
          "analysis": "The sample is a DDoS bot for the ARMv7 architecture. It daemonizes itself by forking and calling `setsid`. The malware then connects to a command and control server to receive instructions. It contains functionality to launch multiple types of DDoS attacks, including various HTTP floods with a large, hardcoded list of user-agents for spoofing, and UDP/TCP floods. The commands to trigger these attacks are parsed in the `processCmd` function and include `OVH`, `UDPRAW`, `STD`, and `XTD`. One specific HTTP flood function, `sendHTTPtwo`, targets Cloudflare-protected sites by sending requests to `/cdn-cgi/l/chk_captchaHTTP/1.1`, indicating an attempt to bypass anti-DDoS measures.",
